Instances of mesh lights authored with primvars:arnold:light

see #2193 and #2437

A point instancer has two mesh light prototypes, authored with primvars:arnold:light: a mesh, and an Xform whose child
mesh inherits the light primvars as written by Solaris. The mesh light is instanced with its mesh, each instance lighting
the grey ground from the instance transform combined with the prototype's one: elongated red pools at the top,
elongated green pools at the bottom. The prototype lights don't emit, the center of the ground stays black.
The legacy usd reader doesn't instance these mesh lights yet, the test is skipped in the 'usd' pass (see the
testsuite groups).

author: cyril.pichard

PARAMS: {'scene': 'scene.usda'}
